WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.801
What's being called an attempted coup

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.770
in the African nation of Sudan.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.271
Residents of the country's capital

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:05.972
say today has been

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.273
the heaviest day of shelling

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.475
since the outbreak of violence

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:10.076
began last week in the United Nations.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.177
Says at least

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.446
180 people were killed

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.748
there over the weekend.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.683
CNN's Nima Elbagir reports for us now.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.885
Even hospitals have come under fire

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:22.822
Sudan's military

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.157
with a show of strength over

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.159
the capital, Khartoum,

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.094
as well

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.865
as birdsong and artillery fire across

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.402
this country roiled in recent years

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.937
by conflict and coups is once again

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.706
the plaything of strongmen.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.474
And what the military is calling

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.710
an attempted coup.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.879
Abdel Fattah Al-burhan, Sudan's military

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.714
leader, is fighting for dominance

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.282
with Mohamed Hamdan Dagalo,

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.350
known as Hamad,

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.985
who leads the paramilitary rapid

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.053
support forces

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.454
which gained notoriety

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.289
in the western Darfur region.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.091
And it is the most vulnerable

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.325
who are paying a price

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:01.761
to doctors.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:02.729
Organizations say

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:03.530
that in Khartoum,

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.330
both sides

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.032
have hit hospitals in the fighting

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:06.566
At least

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:09.069
half a dozen, though both sides deny it.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.472
CNN obtained eyewitness accounts

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:13.073
from doctors

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:13.940
on the ground

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.941
who told CNN

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:17.010
that the paramilitary rapid support force

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.412
directly targeted a hospital

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.481
where wounded armed forces soldiers

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.616
and their families were being treated,

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.051
including one doctor

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.787
who says she witnessed the ISAF approach.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.956
And MAALIM Hospital in central Khartoum

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.058
relaxed, sending my husband understand

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:32.492
I mean,

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.593
I have to be strong enough

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.461
to speak to you.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:35.328
You're the one that's going

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.363
to tell the world what's happening to us.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.299
The evacuation was chaos.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:40.133
We were running

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.202
as soldiers were shouting, run.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.203
And then someone else would

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.737
yell, Stop, it's not safe.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:45.872
But what choice did we have

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:50.443
Three separate

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.144
doctors there

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:51.911
describe to us

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.347
coming under intense bombardment.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:54.848
The country's

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.082
central committee of doctors

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:57.617
tells CNN that with no doctors

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.451
to tell them,

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.552
the dead and injured

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.788
are left to rot in their beds.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.590
And the Sudan Doctors Trade Union

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.391
called the targeting of hospitals

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.260
and the housing of military personnel.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.195
The a clear breach

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.397
of international humanitarian law.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.466
A charge both sides deny

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:16.970
Both military leaders now

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:17.837
fighting for control

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.872
were key allies

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.373
in subverting the country's

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.641
nascent democracy.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.043
After the popular uprising in 2019,

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.812
which deposed Sudan's longtime

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.647
dictator Omar al-Bashir,

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.416
who now languishes in prison.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.085
The memories of those protests

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.386
and the symbolic photo

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:33.820
that became

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.888
its emblem

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:35.889
are slowly fading,

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.891
as has the promised transition

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:38.892
from military

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:41.060
to democratic civilian rule.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.529
Another said on Monday on Saturday.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.230
But in an

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.265
interview with CNN

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:46.132
from Inside

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.001
Army HQ, the leader of Sudan's

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.102
military tells me

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.670
that the RPF militia

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.674
is staging an attempted coup with I'm

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.377
still not happy with my earlier

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.548
as we head into the campaign.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.683
I want to

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.020
give Monken a shot.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:07.720
I asked him

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.856
why the Sudanese people should trust him,

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.358
given his previous partnership

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:15.428
with Commander Dexter in a shop where

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.798
in Sudan where

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.801
the US will play.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.837
General Burhan also committed

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:28.107
to a return to civilian rule.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.943
The leader of the rapid support forces

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:32.612
also told CNN this weekend that he wanted

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.948
to ensure Democratic rule

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.282
that I don't want

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.884
to be the leader of the Army.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.052
There's a framework agreement

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:41.054
between all the Sudanese stakeholders

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.789
that should be adhered to.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:43.990
I don't want to lead anything

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.160
Neither General could tell

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.361
us when the people of Sudan

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.930
could expect this deadly fight to end.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.533
While many languish without water,

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.702
food, electricity,

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:59.138
and no way to bury their dead.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.274
Secretary of State Antony Blinken

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.443
has repeated his calls for calm,

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:05.144
joining other world leaders

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:07.580
but neither he nor those

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.881
standing alongside him

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.983
in these calls

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.017
appear to have any way

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.285
to deliver on them currently.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.120
And there really is no end in sight

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:14.954
at the moment. Jake.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:15.154
All right.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:15.755
Now, Barker,

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:16.489
thank you so much for

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:17.423
that report as always.

